        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(dashboard): stitch session dashboards end-to-end — live provider, show_widget pin, board commands",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe stitch: connects the landed session-dashboard pieces (gateway domain #110960, board view #110644, shell #110728, widget card #110740, core show_widget #110475) into a working end-to-end feature (design: `docs/web/dashboard-architecture.md`).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Real `BoardProvider` in the Control UI: `board.get`/`board.update`/`board.widget.grant` (revision-bound) over the socket, `board.changed` refresh with single-widget iframe reload, `board.command` handling for agent-driven tab focus and chat-dock moves, ticketed `frameUrl` renewal on expiry.\n- `show_widget` gains `name`/`pin`/`tab`/`size`/`after`: pinning stores the same wrapped document bytes on the session board via a server-side canvas-doc copy (`content: {kind:\"canvas-doc\"}` — no client byte shuttling).\n- Transcript widget cards get the **Pin to dashboard** affordance; board cells show `declaredSummary` on grant cards; unpin verified end-to-end.\n- Shell fixes from review: queued `/reset` now routes through the board confirmation; docked chat derives rail/sidebar layout from dock width.\n- UI board types re-pointed to `@openclaw/gateway-protocol`; local duplicates deleted.\n- Store fix (read path): a pre-existing agent DB without board tables now reads as \"no boards\" instead of erroring before the lazy DDL has ever run.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSession dashboards become usable end-to-end: agent shows a widget → pin → board face with docked chat → agent updates by name → live reload. English strings only (locale refresh workflow owns bundles).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused matrix 398 passed (+ new read-path parity coverage, 17/17); Chromium E2E happy path; final autoreview clean; `git diff --check` clean.\n- `check-changed` green through formatting; the final manifest gate showed unrelated drift from #111189 on main at the time — revalidated at land.\n- Contract amendments recorded in the design doc lineage: `canvas-doc` content source, pin vocabulary/result metadata, pending/rejected serving rules. `net` CSP and MCP-app pinning are the two remaining program PRs (T5/T7).\n",
